Sweep the example bodies and compare assembly message types by identity

Dev accepted, in these words: "Accepted, build it" — the recommendation being that the twelve example
definitions the compact form changes be swept as the canonical corpus was swept on 2026-10-21 (their
JSON compacted with `uses` records, their drake surfaces re-emitted, their Scala regenerated and pinned
by the example gate, the other 36 untouched), together with `AssemblyValidator` comparing a consumer's
message type with the actor's by IDENTITY through the definition's record instead of by text, and one
assembly test over a compact definition. No other engine change.

What the sweep is. The October 21 sweep compacted 132 definitions — every main definition and the
staged dreams and service definitions — and left the example domains out, so they were the one part of
the corpus still spelled as authored: an unswept file gains its imports only under a scope, the
asymmetry the sweep removed elsewhere. MEASURED before recommending, with a probe over the compiled
classes compacting all 48 example definitions through the example caller scope (ExampleScope's
identities and bindings): twelve change and gain a record — the four Creators, the four OriginateReports,
aerial Input, terrestrial Output, world Consumer and Provider — and 36 are unchanged, spelling only
own-package and host names. What shortens: `draco.format.dracon.Dracon` to `Dracon` in the Creators' and
Output's consumer parameter and the OriginateReports' consumer binding (the host text inside
`ctx.getRuntime().get[draco.format.dracon.Dracon => Unit]` keeps its spelling, being host-opaque);
`domains.world.World` to `World` in Input's `worldConsumer` (another package, recorded) and in
Consumer's and Provider's parameter and `Actor(World)` header (own package, bare and unrecorded);
`domains.aerial.Position` and `domains.terrestrial.Location` in Consumer's case branch and Input's
binding; and the factory's result `ActorType`, recorded as `draco ActorType`, as the dreams Editor's and
Initialization's records already carry it. Anchors stay in full: Output's `messageType domains world
World`, every derivation line, the domain pointers.

